1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,629
Mira led us through changing terrain.

2
00:00:02,579 --> 00:00:11,011
The landscape was like a tiny continent: a cave opened below a cliff, a glacier shone far above us, and a river ran toward a swamp and a delta.

3
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:12,886
I picked up a pebble.

4
00:00:12,886 --> 00:00:14,909
Is this valuable ore?

5
00:00:14,909 --> 00:00:16,431
I asked.

6
00:00:16,431 --> 00:00:18,818
Mira held a magnet near it.

7
00:00:18,818 --> 00:00:21,579
One test is not enough,’ she said.

8
00:00:21,579 --> 00:00:26,329
At camp, we used a mineral chart to compare quartz, granite and marble.

9
00:00:26,329 --> 00:00:29,534
A red mark on another rock was iron oxide.

10
00:00:29,534 --> 00:00:33,068
Suddenly, even a small stone had a story to tell.

